WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.400
We could just be puh-dump- oh my god.

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:06.980
We could just be dumping water, somewhere not knowing where it goes.

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:25.900
Today we are getting visited by Sawyer Hartman.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:30.360
He's another YouTuber who's actually more of a filmmaker, director personality

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.400
which is really cool. There's a not a whole lot of those on YouTube.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.860
I'm really looking forward to getting to hang out with him a little bit, getting to meet him

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:39.460
now I think he's coming over because he saw the VR backpack video that we made

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:42.480
And he's really excited to try it out. And I'm kind of worried

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:45.100
because. I don't really have it one hundred percent up and running yet.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:46.180
*laughs*

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:55.940
I just walked into the studio and it was just pouring now it's starting to dribble.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.080
What the frack?

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:02.920
This one was doing it yesterday.

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:06.960
Here's the question. How many AC units do you have to install, where two-

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.560
*Off-camera barking* I know, Bandit. I know.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:13.240
Where two out of the three, leak water. When you get done with them.

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:16.700
That means he's got a 67% failure rate on installation.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:18.240
How many times have you done this?

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:21.920
Uh Jake. We have an issue.

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:26.400
There's a pipe in the tool room that's leaking water all over the shelves.

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:28.060
In our tool room?

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:28.560
Yes. :/

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:30.780
So now there's a puddle in the tool room.

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:32.220
Whaaat?

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:35.120
Drip. Like drip drip drip drip drip drip drip.

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:42.240
Ahhh, fuck.

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:45.740
Wren: That's what I heard I was walking by and that's what I heard.

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:47.400
Jake: It'll drip and then it'll stop.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:48.340
And then it'll start again...

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:53.640
So, let's go first to the roof to cut off the source of the problem.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:56.520
An AC unit leaks water, because it's an inverter.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:02:00.320
And all the cool air turns to water and yeah it has to get rid of it.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:06.160
So usually there's an exit pipe that you either filter into a garden or into the sewer, whatever.

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:08.860
Does that look like it might be going somewhere?

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:13.920
Where do you think that's going?

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:15.480
Into our tool room! &gt;:/

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:16.320
That's

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:19.020
This is. Yeah this has to be it.

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:21.960
These air conditioning units are supposed to last for years.

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:28.940
The solution being, let's run piping, without securing it across the roof, to a place we don't know where it goes

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:31.380
Without actually clamping it down

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:33.620
Cmike: Hey man he's only been doing it for 30 years.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:34.820
That's the thing, dude.

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:36.300
I don't- That's what I don't get.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:43.680
My dad was a union carpenter for like 25 years and it's this kind of shit that when he came home,

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.400
when I was a child and he was upset

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:48.080
and I didn't understand why

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:50.080
It's because of this kind of shit.

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:52.060
And now I get it.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:56.320
So, Sam's still in Iceland, and Jake and I have a whole bunch of work we gotta do

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:57.980
To try and get these bigger projects off the ground.

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:00.240
So we need some help to pull off the next video.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:02.780
Now Gabe has a bit of an animation background.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:05.000
And Wren obviously has a great visual background

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:06.360
And Peter...

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:08.880
No one knows what his background is actually like.

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:13.540
But the thing is we asked them to get together and design the stop motion action scene

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:14.240
for the next video.

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:18.500
Curious to see what they come up with. I'm sure it'll be a mish-mash of a bunch of different cool ideas.

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:27.520
Okay so. From the ground I can see both walls and where the cross beam meets the wall.

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:32.080
I wanna find like the cross between enough resolution but also enough coverage.

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:36.640
So we wanna shoot the whole entire thing in here and we wanna do it with no visual effects.

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:38.200
Or at least no visible VFX.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:41.580
You had a good idea to actually attach some sort of dolly system to the rafter up there

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:44.500
So we can move the camera. But, it would be way easier if we didn't have to move the camera at all.

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:46.220
And just shoot wide enough to cover everything.

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:53.300
Good to see you. How are you doing?

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:56.960
But yeah like I mostly make narratives. I made a feature film last year.

00:03:56.960 --> 00:04:02.200
But 88 days ago now, I decided to make a film every single day for 391 days.

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:02.980
391?

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:05.220
Yeah. Every day until my 27th brithday.

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:05.840
Oh, okay.

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:08.600
So now that's kind of like, taken over my life.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:11.360
What's your schedule like when you have to put a video out everyday?

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:15.380
Depends what I'm doing. I always try to structure them like three act stories.

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:17.300
Like get a good chunk of it in the morning

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:19.560
Find the meat in the story in the afternoon

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:21.000
And get the wrap up at night.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:23.240
So I really enjoy showing people VR for the first time.

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:25.820
I've gotten to do it quite a bit now which is great.

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:28.260
And pretty much always people's minds are blown.

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:32.640
And it doesn't matter if you are my mom who has never touched video games before in her life.

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:35.320
Or if you are one of my friends who plays video games all the time.

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:37.260
It all has the same reaction.

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:40.480
Watching people yell and scream and laugh and take off their headset

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:45.120
And like realize they're still in the real world and like come to terms with whether or not they know

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:48.860
If they're actually in the real world... That's the best part.

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:51.800
Holy crap.

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:55.660
It's so weird to like "step out of it?"... yeah

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:58.120
Yeah back to reality? "yeah."

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:00.160
Dude, that was so amazingly cool.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:00.940
What's happening?

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:05.000
The air conditioning guys messed up again

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:09.020
They came to me of course, to fix it, clean it, whatever needs to be done.

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:13.160
My concern is that the water's gotten into the walls

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:15.900
So I'd be interested to see what Gabe, comes back with.

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:19.900
If he doesn't dry it all out. Then we're gonna have mold get in there and that's not a good thing.

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:27.340
We pretty much caught it, before it caused any real damage.

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:33.560
If Wren hadn't just walked by and heard the water falling, then this place would've been flooded.

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:37.360
Since he caught it I think just when it started, that saved me from a lot of work.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:41.900
What I don't understand is why is he using copper pipe of all metals?

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:43.780
Cmike: What's the problem with copper?

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:45.060
Copper's expensive.

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:49.860
We could just be dumping water, somewhere, not knowing where it goes.

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:52.940
How is this okay? Now what do we do with these?

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:57.240
And look it how much unnecessary extra piping he used.

00:05:57.240 --> 00:05:58.940
Did he charge us for all that piping?

00:05:58.940 --> 00:05:59.680
You know he did, dude.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:04.440
Yeah it's just zip-tied like that. That's his "five year solution".

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:08.860
Because there's no more money in the budget, then why didn't he just quote me higher?

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:13.100
Like I want it done right. I don't want i done, super cheap.

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:16.460
So I mean the gist of it is like alright this guy is walking his dog

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:17.960
and some soldier comes out of nowhere.

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:21.120
And then a fight begins. We choreograph that how we want

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:24.740
but in order to realistically, figure out what we're gonna be doing we have to know our bounds.

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:28.020
and our bounds is where the field of view of the camera ends.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:32.240
and we now know that with this set up, I think we can get the entire room.

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:35.760
So I think now that we have a pretty good idea of how we're gonna be filming this stuff

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:37.280
we should figure out what we're gonna be filming.

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:37.780
So Gabe-

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:40.080
Peter: I think we should start story boarding :|

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:43.260
Took the words right out my mouth.

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:44.520
We should start story boarding.

